{"title":"2010 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1(algebra_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1(algebra solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_by_MathTalks\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video by MathTalks</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The lengths of the sides of a triangle in inches are three consecutive integers. The length of the shortest side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the perimeter. What is the length of the longest side?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230da6f41565fda568380a1ce9094eebc7868e66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.28algebra_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1(algebra_solution)\">Solution 1(algebra solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1(algebra solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> be the lengths of the sides of the triangle. Then the perimeter of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad52cfb3d3c523d0a3586780590d4c8306984b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + (n+1) + (n+2) = 3n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"245\" height=\"20\" />. Using the fact that the length of the smallest side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the perimeter, it follows that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b408149a753e773a7e683468a2a6106a3c855db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 0.3(3n+3) \\Rightarrow n = 0.9n+0.9 \\Rightarrow 0.1n = 0.9 \\Rightarrow n=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"448\" height=\"18\" />. The longest side is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/869206d339d7f29546431705c31af7566703ebd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/449203834c58e7dfe000d4da20984a25f6b23c43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" /> is correct.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the length of the shortest side is a whole number and is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0cf2a41ca6fbaafe3d21b823a9bed30c7272fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of the perimeter, it follows that the perimeter must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Adding the two previous integers to each answer choice, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d30b8a3dff23e52f92dbe3a2cf394ee1ab1a1823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11+10+9=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/449203834c58e7dfe000d4da20984a25f6b23c43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" /> is correct.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_by_MathTalks\">Video by MathTalks</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video by MathTalks\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6hRHZxSieKc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6hRHZxSieKc</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 8\">2010 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2010\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\